{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '455,485p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md; sed -n '320,350p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '455,485p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md; sed -n '320,350p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n## 8. Risks and owner decisions\n\nRisks include divergence from front-end tail flags, exact scalar spelling,\nnamed-VM environment leakage, malformed bound operands, source-map loss, and\nUCF's deferred transport contract.\n\nOwner decisions, ranked by B0 blocking impact:\n\n1. B0 blocker: which stable identity, if any, replaces emitter-local tempids\n   in the decoded lossless record DAG.\n2. B0 blocker: the exact result, error, closure, continuation, and stream\n   normalizer.\n3. B0 blocker: whether non-`:yin` attributes belong in the decoded diagnostic\n   side area or are explicitly outside the input domain.\n4. B1 decision: approve the executable scalar domain and\n   `:yin.debruijn.code/*` descriptor.\n5. B5 decision: fix the named VM environment leak or formally exclude it from\n   cross-program park/resume parity fixtures.\n6. B6 decision: authority ledger and trust/provenance, SCC identity, and\n   request-stream retry, timeout, and permanent-absence policy. The linker\n   boundary and local/remote transport are already fixed as `dao.stream`.\n7. Later decision: whether source-to-projection lineage is persisted.\n\n## 9. What this design must not change\n\nThe AST schema, AST walker, named emitter, named linearizer, semantic VM,\nexisting `:yin.code/*` dimension, `dao.stream` protocols, lease layer, waitset,\nnamed storage, projection algorithm, and projection fingerprint remain\nunchanged. The executable encoding and VM are additional artifacts.\nCompare `ast->datoms` -> projection metadata plus B2 -> de Bruijn VM against\n`ast->datoms` -> `linearize/lower` -> semantic VM. Use the actual parity and\ncontent/completion corpora, not helper-only tests as execution fixtures.\nCompletion requires alpha-equivalent programs to share projection identity\nwhile their executable images may differ, and all three host lanes to agree\nunder the normalizer.\n\n### B6: optional linked stream topology\n\n    New files only, after an owner decision\n    Existing edits: none by default\n    Must not change: projection fingerprint or local VM semantics\n\nAdd a separate linked dimension and stream process for `:call-hash`: park a\ncontinuation, emit a request, verify arriving content, load it, and resume.\nCompletion requires cycle-safe manifests, explicit authority, gap/timeout\noutcomes, and hash-mismatch diagnostics. The local VM remains link-agnostic.\n\n## 7. Test matrix and non-goals\n\nThe matrix includes inverse encoding, exact scalar spelling, names, tail flags,\nprovenance, scope, duplicate parameters, nil fill, extras dropped, control\nflow, streams, effects, continuations, macros, malformed images, and all\nexisting parity/content/completion execution fixtures. It also includes\nalpha-equivalent equal projections with distinct executable images, free-name\nchanges, and cross-host code-image bytes.\n\nNon-goals are equality saturation, a new JIT, global distribution, dependency\nhash linking before B6, and any change to the projection or its fingerprint.\n\n### 7.1 Prior art: Unison's runtime\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
